# Taskboard CLI

A dependency-free TypeScript task manager for [Bun](https://bun.sh/). Each invocation writes exactly one JSON value to stdout; errors also produce a short diagnostic on stderr and a non-zero exit status.

## Usage

Run commands from the project directory:

```sh
bun run src/cli.ts add --title "Ship release" --tags work,urgent --due 2026-09-10
bun run src/cli.ts list --status open --tag urgent
bun run src/cli.ts list --overdue 2026-09-11
bun run src/cli.ts done 1
bun run src/cli.ts delete 1
bun run src/cli.ts stats
```

Data is stored in `.taskboard.json` in the current directory. Set `TASKBOARD_FILE` to use another path:

```sh
TASKBOARD_FILE=/tmp/my-tasks.json bun run src/cli.ts list
```

Tags are trimmed, lowercased, and deduplicated. Dates must be real calendar dates in `YYYY-MM-DD` format. `--overdue DATE` selects open tasks due strictly before that date; `stats` compares against today's local date.

Writes use a temporary sibling file followed by an atomic rename. Existing malformed data causes the command to fail and is never silently replaced.

## Tests

```sh
bun test
```

The end-to-end suite starts separate Bun processes and covers persistence, monotonic IDs, normalization, combined filters, overdue boundaries, idempotency, errors, statistics, and malformed-database preservation.
